Clear and explicit guarding of constraints by system mode is essential to avoid contradictory or vacuous verification results. User preferences indicate that abstract modeling of simultaneity and temporal aspects is sufficient, with soft constraints verified by assertions providing a flexible balance between enforcement and feasibility. Explicit documentation of abstractions and mode-conditional constraints enables clearer specifications and successful formal verification.

