- Always explicitly guard facts with mode conditions to avoid contradictory or vacuous constraints.  
- Soft constraints should be modeled as facts or predicates but verified via assertions to avoid blocking valid behaviors.  
- Temporal modeling with `Time` requires ordering and no direct arithmetic; use ordering predicates to relate times.  
- Incremental predicates and assertions facilitate stepwise verification and early detection of inconsistencies.

