- Mode-guard all constraints (facts) explicitly to avoid contradictory or vacuous constraints across system modes.  
- Soft constraints (such as credential update requirements) can be modeled as facts but are verified via assertions to avoid blocking system behavior.  
- Temporal relations use ordering from `util/ordering[Time]` but do not support direct arithmetic on abstract `Time` atoms.

